====================================================================================================
CALIBRATION at h=1: does a bigger predicted move mean a bigger real one?
====================================================================================================
    predicted move (c)        n   mean realised (c)    ratio
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                -10.94      215               -2.47     0.23
                 -3.32      146               -0.42     0.13
                 -1.25       95                0.45    -0.36
                 -0.01       71               -1.97   350.72
                  1.24      108               -0.00    -0.00
                  3.38      202                0.91     0.27
                 12.56      562                2.25     0.18
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ratio 1.0 = perfectly calibrated: predicted 5c move, realised 5c move.
  ratio near 0 with good direction = the SIGN is informative but the
  SIZE is not, and only size is tradeable -- the same failure mode as
  the coverage extension in section 4 of the results document.
  A ratio that is consistently positive and rising across buckets is the
  result that would justify resting limit orders at the model's estimate.
